# Mouse controls (v1.29.0), port/tools/mousecheck.sh scenarios "pixel", "fill" and "stretch" (format:
# attack_e16.mouse): WINDOW pixels, the same file under each Scaling mode, with the window made 1200x500 first.
# Start: as attack_e16.mouse (camera (112,272)). mousecheck.sh writes MODE lines' events for its mode only
# ("@pixel", "@fill", "@stretch" prefixes; the others for all). Picture pixel (200,40), square (19,19), is window
# pixel (240 + 3 x 200 + 1.5, 10 + 3 x 40 + 1.5) in Pixel (3x, 720x480 at 240,10), (225 + 3.125 x 200 + 1.5,
# 3.125 x 40 + 1.5) in Fill (3.125x, 750x500 at 225,0), (5 x 200 + 2.5, 3.125 x 40 + 1.5) in Stretch. Window
# pixel (100,250) is on the left black bar in Pixel and Fill (no key), and picture pixel (20,80) in Stretch.
7930 size 1200 500
@pixel 7940 click left 841.5 131.5
@fill 7940 click left 851.5 126.5
@stretch 7940 click left 1002.5 126.5
7990 click left 100 250
